  message: "DEPENDENCY NOTE: WI-toruz carries a re-evaluation trigger keyed on THIS item's ruling. WI-toruz rules call_construct=constructor CANONICAL on instantiates edges, and its stated reason is that the value is the only cross-language invariant for object creation that survives the edge_type disagreement documented here. If this item is ruled such that ONE edge_type carries all object creation across every language, then constructor becomes derivable from edge_type and WI-toruz's Keep verdict flips to a fold. Whoever rules this item should re-read WI-toruz before closing."  # 92b2
